1
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:39,750
The album that changed it all.

2
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:13,500
Thriller 40 is a documentary, music film directed by Nelson George.

3
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:47,250
Forty years after the release of Michael Jackson’s ‘Thriller,’ the best-selling album of all-time, director Nelson George takes
fans back in time to the making of a pop masterpiece, featuring never-before-seen footage and candid interviews.

4
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:21,000
Self (archive footage), played by Michael Jackson.

5
00:27:48,750 --> 00:27:54,750
Self (archive footage), played by Quincy Jones.

6
00:33:22,500 --> 00:33:28,500
Self (archive footage), played by Paul McCartney.

7
00:38:56,250 --> 00:39:02,250
Self, played by Usher.

8
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:36,000
Self, played by Mary J. Blige.

9
00:50:03,750 --> 00:50:09,750
Self, played by Mark Ronson.

10
00:55:37,500 --> 00:55:43,500
Thriller 40 is a 2023 documentary film about the 40th
anniversary of Michael Jackson's 1982 album Thriller.

11
01:01:11,250 --> 01:01:17,250
The film, directed by Nelson George, was released in
the United States on December 2, 2023.

12
01:06:45,000 --> 01:06:51,000
It aired on Showtime and was streamed on
Paramount+ only for Showtime subscribers.

13
01:12:18,750 --> 01:12:24,750
Internationally, it debuted the same day in the U.K., Australia, Canada, Italy,
France, Germany, Switzerland, Austria, Latin America, and South Korea.

14
01:17:52,500 --> 01:17:58,500
On October 27, 2023, the trailer for the documentary was released.

15
01:23:26,250 --> 01:23:32,250
A 40th-anniversary edition reissue of Thriller (1982)
of the same title was released in 2022.
